-- Tests of l4/laws/contracts-law.l4 (MMS-529): how §25 reads the corpus's
-- kinds of instrument, and what §§26 and 61 give. They sit beside the
-- module and not in it (the client, 2026-10-22).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `contracts-law`

§ `בדיקות חוק החוזים`

-- Every agreement the corpus holds was made before 7.1.2026: the earlier
-- text reads it, by the parties' intent, and by its language where the
-- intent appears explicitly from it.
`a collective agreement of 2008` MEANS `contract section 25 reads` WITH
    `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026` IS FALSE
    `its kind` IS `an employment contract or a collective agreement, as section 25 counts it`
    `the parties agreed how it is read` IS FALSE
    `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it` IS TRUE
    `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense` IS FALSE
    `its language alone sets its provisions against each other` IS FALSE
    `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language` IS FALSE

`a collective agreement of 2008 whose words settle it` MEANS `contract section 25 reads` WITH
    `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026` IS FALSE
    `its kind` IS `an employment contract or a collective agreement, as section 25 counts it`
    `the parties agreed how it is read` IS FALSE
    `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it` IS TRUE
    `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense` IS FALSE
    `its language alone sets its provisions against each other` IS FALSE
    `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the way section 25 reads it` `a collective agreement of 2008` EQUALS `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`
#ASSERT `the way section 25 reads it` `a collective agreement of 2008 whose words settle it` EQUALS `by its language, the parties' intent appearing explicitly from it`

-- The same agreement signed after 7.1.2026, its words explicit or not, is
-- read by the parties' intent under (4): the explicit-language limb is
-- gone from the new text.
`a collective agreement of 2026 whose words settle it` MEANS `contract section 25 reads` WITH
    `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026` IS TRUE
    `its kind` IS `an employment contract or a collective agreement, as section 25 counts it`
    `the parties agreed how it is read` IS FALSE
    `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it` IS TRUE
    `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense` IS FALSE
    `its language alone sets its provisions against each other` IS FALSE
    `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the way section 25 reads it` `a collective agreement of 2026 whose words settle it` EQUALS `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`

-- A business contract of 2026 whose parties agreed how it is read, but
-- without a lawyer: (5)(א) counts no agreement, so its language alone
-- reads it — until that language gives a result that makes no sense.
`a business contract of 2026 agreed without a lawyer` MEANS `contract section 25 reads` WITH
    `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026` IS TRUE
    `its kind` IS `a business contract, as section 25 counts it`
    `the parties agreed how it is read` IS TRUE
    `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it` IS FALSE
    `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense` IS FALSE
    `its language alone sets its provisions against each other` IS FALSE
    `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language` IS FALSE

`a business contract of 2026 whose language makes no sense` MEANS `contract section 25 reads` WITH
    `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026` IS TRUE
    `its kind` IS `a business contract, as section 25 counts it`
    `the parties agreed how it is read` IS FALSE
    `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it` IS TRUE
    `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense` IS TRUE
    `its language alone sets its provisions against each other` IS FALSE
    `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the way section 25 reads it` `a business contract of 2026 agreed without a lawyer` EQUALS `by its language alone`
#ASSERT `the way section 25 reads it` `a business contract of 2026 whose language makes no sense` EQUALS `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`

-- A standard contract is read by intent even where it says otherwise.
`a standard contract of 2026 that sets its own way` MEANS `contract section 25 reads` WITH
    `made or renewed on or after 7.1.2026` IS TRUE
    `its kind` IS `a standard contract, as section 25 counts it`
    `the parties agreed how it is read` IS TRUE
    `both parties had a lawyer in drafting it` IS TRUE
    `its language alone gives a result that makes no sense` IS FALSE
    `its language alone sets its provisions against each other` IS FALSE
    `the parties' intent appears explicitly from its language` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the way section 25 reads it` `a standard contract of 2026 that sets its own way` EQUALS `by the parties' intent, as it appears from the contract and the circumstances`

-- (ב) and (ב1).
`a reading that keeps it, for the drafter` MEANS `reading of a contract under section 25` WITH
    `keeps the contract in force` IS TRUE
    `favours the party that had the upper hand in shaping its terms` IS TRUE
`a reading that voids it, against the drafter` MEANS `reading of a contract under section 25` WITH
    `keeps the contract in force` IS FALSE
    `favours the party that had the upper hand in shaping its terms` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `section 25(ב) prefers the one reading to the other` `a reading that keeps it, for the drafter` `a reading that voids it, against the drafter`
#ASSERT `section 25(ב1) prefers the one reading to the other` `a reading that voids it, against the drafter` `a reading that keeps it, for the drafter` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 25(ב1) prefers the one reading to the other` `a reading that voids it, against the drafter` `a reading that keeps it, for the drafter` FALSE

-- (ד) applies seven sections of the Interpretation Law.
#ASSERT `section 25(ד) applies those sections` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 25(ד) applies those sections` TRUE FALSE

-- §26: the practice between the parties first.
#ASSERT `the source section 26 gives a missing detail` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `from the practice between the parties`
#ASSERT `the source section 26 gives a missing detail` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `from the practice usual in contracts of that kind`
#ASSERT `the source section 26 gives a missing detail` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 26 gives it no source`

-- §61: an agreement as a contract, a circular under (ב).
#ASSERT `how section 61 brings the Contracts Law to it` `a contract: an agreement or a teacher's contract of employment` FALSE EQUALS `as a contract`
#ASSERT `how section 61 brings the Contracts Law to it` `a legal act that is not a contract: a circular, the takanon or a letter` FALSE EQUALS `under section 61(ב), so far as it suits the matter`
#ASSERT `how section 61 brings the Contracts Law to it` `a contract: an agreement or a teacher's contract of employment` TRUE EQUALS `not: another law provides specially for the matter`
